{"name":"Coffee Bag","hex":"#dbd6d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coffee bag","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A container used for shipping and storing coffee.","A small gauze bag containing a mixture of instant coffee and finely ground roast coffee, infused to make coffee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee_bag"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffee bag","blocks":[{"text":"A coffee bag is a container for shipping and storing coffee. Coffee beans are usually transported in large jute sacks, while coffee sold to consumers may be packaged as beans or ground coffee in a small, sealed plastic bag."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sacos_de_caf%C3%A9%2C_Casa_do_Bandeirante_2.JPG/330px-Sacos_de_caf%C3%A9%2C_Casa_do_Bandeirante_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_bag","wikidata":"Q28051230"},{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee","wikidata":"Q8486"},{"title":"Bag","blocks":[{"text":"A bag, also known regionally as a sack or tote, is a common tool in the form of a floppy container, typically made of cloth, leather, bamboo, paper, or plastic. The use of bags predates recorded history, with the earliest bags being lengths of animal skin, cotton, or woven plant fibers, folded up at the edges and secured in that shape with strings of the same material. Bags can be used to carry items such as personal belongings, groceries, tools, and other objects. They come in various shapes and sizes, often equipped with handles or straps for easier carrying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg/330px-Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bag","wikidata":"Q1323314"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)","wikidata":"Q2932937"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Bags_of_coffee.jpg/500px-Bags_of_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Bags_of_coffee.jpg/500px-Bags_of_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pre-packaged bags of coffee beans and ground coffee at supermarket","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABags_of_coffee.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Counter_Culture_Coffee_Bag.jpg/120px-Counter_Culture_Coffee_Bag.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Counter_Culture_Coffee_Bag.jpg/250px-Counter_Culture_Coffee_Bag.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Counter_Culture_Coffee_Bag.jpg/120px-Counter_Culture_Coffee_Bag.jpg?utm_source=e